For probe history, distinguish active executable probe shape from inert historical evidence bytes if the existing law supports that distinction; otherwise sustain the conflict. For authority identity and review target, judge the actual bootstrap artifacts rather than accepting intent. Decide whether issue/material duplication, legacy-import coupling, repository-reference clump, and “one invocation” naming are real construction blockers or nonblocking smells.

Return the smallest exact repair scope. Do not edit artifacts, route roles, or require Recorder implementation evidence in this Review posture. Do not inspect archived session payloads.

