    "summary": "At exact HEAD 87457469250260d99d7df4b44cbb110fa274ad26, three defects require only append-only documentary repair; no Recorder implementation proof is due.

Dispositions: (1) Probe-lifecycle violation rejected: CLAUDE.md forbids retaining an active scratch/executable probe shape or duplicate behavior, but not inert historical evidence bytes. Legacy import may preserve such bytes only inertly; it may not install a standalone runnable/discoverable probe, and graduation/deletion law still applies to the active probe. (2) Invocation finding sustained only as a contract wording defect; executing a caller-selected command is not package-owned role composition. (3) Authority-input sealing sustained: both Judge bootstrap manifests actually omit required input digests. (4) Review-target mismatch sustained: target.json actually says 71e8a5aabe1dee5c7340a19a0e80db376c77621a while the manifest and Receipt bind 49796e44202e8024c712b0e50a482f7882cf30cd. Duplicated issue.json/materials.md is preserved bootstrap evidence, not a new mechanism; do not rewrite it. The owner-required legacy migration is explicitly contributor work outside Recorder runtime, so it is not divergent module ownership. The repository reference tuple is a coherent identity value whose implementation naming is Apply-local. “One invocation” is a real naming ambiguity but is fully cured by the seam clarification below.

Smallest repair:
1. Add one forward authority clarification: the Recorder accepts one exact caller-supplied argv command plus caller-supplied execution context and executes it exactly once as a mechanical capture wrapper. It may not select, synthesize, alter, retry, compose, or route commands. The caller owns semantic dispatch; the package owns only spawn/capture, archive processing, and separate child-outcome reporting. An externally produced event-stream-only interface is not required. Preserve the already-frozen archive-failure precedence and Receipt non-interpretation rules.
2. Add one append-only bootstrap correction record; do not rewrite accepted manifests. Seal Judge-001 input `.ak/dockets/issues/10/authority/materials.md` as SHA-256 `54f5522f47a52d87d8a6fcaa81a50ab3707de109a53ff371bf6df7b541d19c5b`. Seal Judge-002 input `.ak/dockets/issues/10/authority/request-002.md` as `e13c973d49b3f7794cb423051987caa7642c4678b749f9a980c7a9516728c3fb`, and its referenced materials/amendment/Judge-001 Receipt as respectively `54f5522f47a52d87d8a6fcaa81a50ab3707de109a53ff371bf6df7b541d19c5b`, `cca7da9f54c13e13e1563de7d5af4b20dd0ca8b0a32bb15afec4f948f4cf94f3`, and `663f2a6dd1aead62225f57b8f8a04eec132f674b2c235fb1eb820304241dff72`.
3. In that same correction trail, explicitly supersede only the stale range assertion in target.json (preserving its bytes and digest `cdd28ae7b8a22ca3a81ec3acc024c39f462d958f87fc64a691cd52d8e9c3cd9a`) and record the actual immutable review range `6e76efa93588844996611b86320de7747cca3d24..49796e44202e8024c712b0e50a482f7882cf30cd`, already corroborated by the bootstrap review manifest and Receipt. No review rerun, artifact deletion, role routing, schema mechanism, or code change is supported."
